# Resume Scoring Tool — Design Fixes

Here's exactly what to change on the landing page. The concept is solid (bank ticker, invite-only gate, IB scoring angle) — it just needs a CSS pass to not read as AI-built.

---

## 1. Fonts (biggest issue)

Right now you're using DM Sans + Instrument Serif italic + DM Mono. That's the exact default combo every AI spits out for "dark premium financial site." Swap to:

- **Body/UI text:** `"IBM Plex Sans"` instead of DM Sans
- **"Unfiltered" accent:** `"Cormorant Garamond"` instead of Instrument Serif
- **Stat labels (18+, 14+, 100):** `"JetBrains Mono"` instead of DM Mono
- **Heading ("Built for IB recruiting"):** `"Helvetica Neue"` or keep IBM Plex Sans at heavier weight

Add tighter letter-spacing (`-0.01em`) on body text — AI defaults leave it too loose.

## 2. The italic accent word

"Built for IB recruiting. *Unfiltered.*" — one gold italic serif word inside a sans-serif heading is an AI layout cliche now. Two options:

- **Option A:** Make the full heading serif. "Built for IB recruiting" in Cormorant Garamond regular, "Unfiltered" in Cormorant Garamond italic + gold color. Same font family, just style shift.
- **Option B:** Keep it sans-serif but use weight contrast. "Built for IB recruiting." in light weight, "Unfiltered." in bold + gold. No font switch at all.

## 3. Border radius — sharpen everything

Right now cards and inputs are ~8-10px radius. That's the AI default rounded look. Change to:

- Form card container: `3px`
- Input fields: `2px`
- "Continue" button: `2px`
- Any other containers: `2px-4px` max

This alone makes a huge difference — gives it that Bloomberg/terminal sharpness.

## 4. Background color

You're using a navy-tinted dark (something like `#0A0C12`). That blue-dark is another AI tell. Go to:

- `#050505` (true near-black) or `#0C0A09` (warm black)
- The form card background: go slightly lighter but still warm, like `#111110` not `#1A1A2E`

## 5. Text colors

Body text is currently a blue-gray (the AI default for dark mode readable text). Swap to warmer tones:

- Body/description text: `#B5B0A8` (warm stone gray)
- Headings: `#EDEDED` (off-white, not pure white)
- "PRIVATE ACCESS ONLY" / "INVITE ONLY" labels: `#8A8578` (warm muted)
- "BANK PROFILES" / "FORMAT CHECKS" stat labels: `#6B6560` (warm dark gray)

## 6. The "Continue →" button

Gold filled button with arrow is very AI-template. Change to:

- **Ghost/outline style:** transparent background, `1px solid #D4A853` border, gold text
- Remove the `→` arrow
- Add `text-transform: uppercase` and `letter-spacing: 0.08em` at `font-size: 13px`
- Or go fully minimal: white text, no background, subtle bottom border only

## 7. The bank ticker at top

This is actually one of the best elements — keep it. One small tweak: the font looks like it might be the default sans-serif. Set it explicitly to `"Helvetica Neue"` or `"IBM Plex Sans"` with `letter-spacing: 0.15em` and `font-weight: 400`. Slightly reduce the font size if it's above 12px — smaller reads more premium/understated.

## 8. Form card

The card itself has a subtle border or shadow. Make sure:

- Border: `1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06)` (very faint, not obvious)
- No box-shadow (AI loves adding `box-shadow` to cards)
- Background: `#0E0E0D` (barely lighter than page, warm)
- "INVITE ONLY" label: smaller font, more letter-spacing, warm gray not white

---

## Copy-Paste CSS

```css
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600&family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400&display=swap');

/* Body / UI — replace DM Sans */
body, p, span, label, input, button {
  font-family: "IBM Plex Sans", "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
}

/* Accent text — replace Instrument Serif */
.accent-text, .italic-highlight {
  font-family: "Cormorant Garamond", Georgia, serif;
}

/* Stats / mono — replace DM Mono */
.stat-number, .stat-label, code {
  font-family: "JetBrains Mono", "SF Mono", monospace;
}

/* Background — true black, not navy */
body {
  background-color: #050505;
}

/* Form card */
.form-card {
  background: #0E0E0D;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  border-radius: 3px;
  box-shadow: none;
}

/* Inputs */
input {
  border-radius: 2px;
  background: #0A0A09;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
}

/* Text colors — warm, not blue-gray */
p, .body-text {
  color: #B5B0A8;
}

h1, h2 {
  color: #EDEDED;
}

.label, .small-text {
  color: #8A8578;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  font-size: 11px;
}

/* CTA button — ghost style */
.cta-button {
  background: transparent;
  border: 1px solid #D4A853;
  color: #D4A853;
  border-radius: 2px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 500;
  padding: 12px 32px;
}

.cta-button:hover {
  background: rgba(212, 168, 83, 0.08);
}

/* Bank ticker */
.ticker {
  font-family: "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
  letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 400;
  color: #6B6560;
}
```

---

The class names above are placeholders — match them to whatever's in the actual codebase. The values are what matter.

